      "text": "We start by listing out the numbers 1 to 6 in a sequence: 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6. Carolyn starts by removing the number 2. Since 2 has no positive divisors other than 1 and itself, it remains.\n\nPaul now removes all the positive divisors of 2, which are just 1. The remaining numbers are 3, 4, 5, and 6.\n\nNext, Carolyn removes the largest remaining number, which is 6. Since 6 has the divisors 1, 2, 3, and 6, Carolyn removes 6.\n\nPaul now removes all of Carolyn's divisors, which are 2. The remaining numbers are 3, 4, and 5.\n\nNext, Carolyn removes the largest remaining number, which is 4. Since 4 has the divisors 1, 2, and 4, Carolyn removes 4.\n\nPaul now removes all of Carolyn's divisors, which are 2. The remaining number is 5.\n\nNext, Carolyn removes the largest remaining number, which is 5. Since 5 has the divisor 1, Carolyn removes 5.\n\nAll remaining numbers have no positive divisors other than themselves, and Paul removes them.\n\nIn total, Carolyn removes the numbers 2, 6, 4, and 5, which sum up to 2 + 6 + 4 + 5 = 17.\n\nHence, the sum of the numbers that Carolyn removes is \\boxed{17}.",
