      "text": "\\begin{align*}\n&\\bullet \\text{ Unless Carolyn removes } n \\text{when she is allowed to, she is able to remove } 2n.\\\\\n&\\because 2 \\text{ is the only positive divisor of } 1, 2 \\text{ is the only number Carolyn can remove initially, and} \\\\\n&\\because \\text { once Carolyn removes } 2, \\text{ all numbers other than } n \\text{ are now odd and have more than one positive divisor,}\\\\\n&\\text { Paul is ultimately forced to leave only } n \\text{ for Carolyn to remove on her subsequent turn,}\\\\\n&\\text { Carolyn can therefore remove } 2n = 12.\\\\\n&\\text{ Carolyn can't remove } 2 < n-2 \\text{ because that would leave fewer than three numbers for Paul and Carolyn can't}\\\\\n&\\text{ remove } n-1 \\text{ because Carolyn can't remove any number afterward.}\\\\\n&\\text{ Carolyn can only remove } 2 \\text{ on her first turn, while the other players can remove multiples of } 2. \\text{ Therefore, the sum of the numbers}\\\\\n&2 + n - 1 + n - 2 +...= n-2+n= n= 6.\\\\\n\\end{align*}",
